## Quick start

1. Install {{PREREQUISITES}}, then create and activate the environment: `conda env create -f envs/workflow.yaml`, then `conda activate {{ENV_NAME}}`.
2. Put raw data in `data/raw/` and record provenance in `data/README.md`.
3. Fill in `config/` (see `config/README.md`).
4. Run: `{{RUN_COMMAND}}`
5. Test: `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`

## Layout

| Folder | Contents |
|--------|----------|
| `config/` | Sample sheet, parameters, reference pins |
| `data/` | `raw/` (immutable), `reference/`, `processed/` |
| `workflow/` | Pipeline definition |
| `scripts/` | Analysis code called by the workflow |
| `notebooks/` | Exploration; anything final moves into `scripts/` |
| `envs/` | Software environment specs |
| `results/` | Generated outputs (reproducible, not hand-edited) |
| `tests/` | Tests for scripts and workflow |
| `docs/` | Decisions, methods notes, principles |

Each folder has a README with Purpose, Conventions, Current state, and Last major change. AI agents start from `AGENTS.md`.
